<p>Argentina are the reigning world champions. They are ranked first in the world. Their squad contains multiple Champions League winners and the most decorated player in the history of the sport. Cape Verde has a population of 560,000 people — roughly the size of Sacramento — and has never before reached the knockout stage of a World Cup. Their goalkeeper plays in the second tier of Portuguese football.</p>
<p>By every objective measure, this should not be a competitive match. Cape Verde held Spain 0-0 in the group stage. Spain was ranked second in the world at the time. <strong>Vozinha has not conceded a single goal at this tournament.</strong> Messi has scored more goals at this tournament than Cape Verde's entire squad combined.</p>
