<div class="callout-text"><strong>The UNICEF photo, now a World Cup matchup:</strong> In December 2007, a 6-month-old Lamine Yamal was photographed with Messi for a charity calendar. That photo became the story of the tournament when Yamal scored his first World Cup goal at 18 and faced Spain in the same competition. But an even more extraordinary coincidence runs parallel: Messi — who leads this tournament in goals — now faces a goalkeeper who was already a professional when that photo was taken. Vozinha was 21 years old in December 2007. Messi was 20. They have spent 19 years playing professional football on opposite sides of the world and are meeting for the first time on Friday in Miami.</div>
