<h2>The Physical Mismatch That Explains Everything</h2>
<p>The most useful way to understand Friday's match athletically is to understand the specific physical contest between Messi and Vozinha — because that is ultimately what the game will hinge on.</p>
<h3>Messi's Physical Advantage Over Vozinha</h3>
<p>Messi's peak recorded speed is approximately 20.2 mph. He reaches that speed in approximately 1.8 to 2.0 seconds from standing — one of the fastest first-step accelerations in professional soccer. When he receives the ball inside the penalty area, he can change direction faster than any defender at his speed because his 5'7" frame has a lower center of gravity than any outfield player marking him.</p>
<p>Against Vozinha specifically: <strong>Messi's preferred finishing position — inside the box, left foot, angled shot across the goalkeeper — is exactly the shot that is most difficult for a 6'2" goalkeeper to cover.</strong> A shorter goalkeeper can get lower faster, but Vozinha is not a short goalkeeper. His standing reach of approximately 7'9" gives him exceptional coverage of the crossbar region, but Messi's trademark placement near the post at keeper height is precisely where Vozinha's reach advantage is most neutralized.</p>
<h3>Vozinha's Physical Advantage Over Messi</h3>
<p>Vozinha makes up what he lacks in pure reaction time (which decreases with age) with positioning. He has 20+ years of reading where forwards will finish from every situation, which means he is typically already in the right starting position before Messi even pulls the trigger. Against Spain, seven of his saves came precisely because he was positioned correctly before the shot happened — not because he reacted faster than the ball. That is a skill that compounds with age rather than declining with it.</p>
<p>His 6'2" standing reach of ~7'9" also means he passively covers more of the goal than a shorter keeper without needing to dive. Messi at 5'7" generates shots from positions where most strikers would shoot low — because that is where his natural body mechanics produce the most power. Those low shots to the near post, which Messi has used his entire career, are shots where Vozinha's height is more advantage than liability.</p>
